+# LEDGER-Q cinematic presentation update
+
+## Scope
+
+Original baseline: `173b7b941533e22187298ec45bb14c68430c8709`. Existing application retained. No database migrations, API implementations, authentication logic, source records, roles, review rules or export rules were changed.
+
+The landing hero now uses an isolated CSS 3D evidence/document assembly with synchronized floating depth, restrained pointer response and reversible scroll movement. Four keyboard-operable explanatory steps clarify the product workflow. The assembly is explicitly illustrative, not saved evidence or an approval. Reduced-motion preferences preserve a static, separated diagram; offscreen/hidden animations pause internally. Existing landing reveals remain reversible; no cinematic motion was added to working evidence.
+
+The historical feature mapping status column now matches the authoritative implementation register. CURRENT_FEATURE_REGISTER.md identifies the authoritative current F01–F20 and 45-item allocation registers. The allocation remains 11 reuse, 24 refinements, five additions and five deferred.
+
+## Executed checks
+
+- TypeScript: passed.
+- Production build: passed.
+- 147 local engineering checks passed across 4 suites; no failing checks. See regression-results.json.
+- Source route inventory preserved: routes-preserved.json.
+- Existing synthetic proof logic, values and demo selection logic retained. Tests cover the saved workflow and its negative conditions.
+
+## Limits
+
+Browser screenshot, live pointer/scroll, mobile visual and 200% zoom QA were not executable in this environment because the required browser-control capability was unavailable. SSR/runtime checks are not a substitute for visual inspection. The motion is adapted from the supplied recording, not an exact copy of its original assets/fonts. No real-user pilot, live model inference, actual Google consent flow or production database inspection was run during this presentation change. Provider/OAuth tests use fixtures. Existing live-provider configuration and maturity labels are not promoted by this update. No accuracy, time-saving or commercial-validation claims were added.
+
+## Deployment
+
+Publish with existing audience and URLs. Presentation code is isolated in components/evidence-choreography.tsx and its CSS module.
